        "subject": "LU-17000 lnet: fix inconsistent NULL handling",
        "message": "LU-17000 lnet: fix inconsistent NULL handling\n\nlnet_compare_gw_lpnis() and lnet_compare_routes() test both arguments\nfor NULL and then dereference both unconditionally, so a call with two\nNULL arguments would crash.  Their only caller,\nlnet_find_route_locked(), always passes a valid first argument - the\nroute being examined and the peer NI it has just checked.  Its second\nargument is NULL until the first route is selected, and only for\nlnet_compare_routes(): lnet_compare_gw_lpnis() is reached only when\nlnet_compare_routes() returned 0, which means best_route is not NULL,\nand best_gw_ni is assigned in the same statement group as best_route.\nThe caller already relies on that by reading best_route->lr_seq right\nthere.  Keep the NULL test lnet_compare_routes() needs, drop the three\ndead ones, and state both contracts in the comments.\n\nlnet_ni_add_interface() computes strlen(iface) in the initialiser of\niface_len, before the !iface test that follows.  Compute the length\nonce the arguments have been validated.\n\nReported by smatch as \"we previously assumed 'lpni1'/'lpni2'/'r1'\ncould be null\" and \"variable dereferenced before check 'iface'\".\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I14f637f46617d92efcaf32fdc2a904a91f202a8c\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68503\nReviewed-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
